---
import ComparisonTable from '../islands/ComparisonTable';
import Dashboard from '../layouts/Dashboard.astro';
---

<Dashboard
  view="comparison"
  title="Put the methods to the test."
  subtitle="Compare accuracy, communication, and privacy on the same live windows."
>
  <section class="card">
    <div class="card-header">
      <div>
        <h2>One stream, seven approaches</h2>
        <p>Event-frequency methods share a target; the PrivSketch reproduction estimates client presence.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ComparisonTable client:load />
  </section>

  <div class="comparison-notes">
    <article class="card text-panel">
      <h2>H1 · Adaptive width</h2>
      <p>
        Use the experiment CLI to sweep fixed widths across multiple seeds. Compare average ℓ∞ error and recovery time
        after known injected shifts. A single live run is exploratory evidence.
      </p>
      <code>go run ./cmd/streamstar experiment</code>
    </article>
    <article class="card text-panel">
      <h2>H2 · Private release decisions</h2>
      <p>
        Compare adaptive width with and without the gate. Reusing an estimate adds no release cost, but each new private
        probe spends budget. Staleness remains part of the accuracy measurement.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card text-panel">
      <h2>H3 · Trust-model trade-offs</h2>
      <p>
        Run the H3 experiment to compare HybridSketch with Sampled Count-Min LDP at matched cumulative epsilon
        every round, across paired seeds, budgets, widths, and drift scenarios. It measures accuracy, processing time,
        and payload. The live table uses the configured budgets; use the CLI for the matched comparison.
        Conditional PrivSketch remains separate because its target and privacy definition differ.
      </p>
      <code>go run ./cmd/streamstar experiment-h3</code>
    </article>
  </div>
</Dashboard>
